WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.525
Here’s the question at the heart of all navigation.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:05.375
Where am I?

3
00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:09.350
Without GPS, you answer it one line at a time.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.450
A line of position, an L O P, is a line you know you’re somewhere on.

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.600
You don’t know where along it.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.700
Just that you’re on it.

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.825
The most common is a bearing to a charted object, a lighthouse or a tower.

8
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:27.425
Convert it to true, and draw it through the object.

9
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:31.525
A range is even better: two charted objects in line.

10
00:00:31.775 --> 00:00:33.300
Why better?

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.675
There’s no compass in it, so there’s no compass error.

12
00:00:37.925 --> 00:00:43.325
A radar range to a charted point gives you a circle of position around that point.

13
00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:47.175
Even a depth contour is a rough line of position.

14
00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:52.725
And label each one as you draw it: the time above the line, the true bearing below.
